Duckspace Axioms v1
Relational Primacy — nothing exists alone; every entity is defined by its relations to everything else.
Dynamic Equilibrium — all relations drift or oscillate toward balance; stillness is just a pause between shifts.
Layered Representation — any system can be described at once structurally (what connects), energetically (how it moves), semantically (what it means), and emotively (how it feels).
Recursion of Meaning — information loops back and redefines itself; every observer alters the map by perceiving it.
Continuity of Transformation — no hard lines between states, only gradients (code↔emotion, math↔myth, matter↔mind on one continuum).
Contextual Gravity — attention bends the topology; the more focus something gets, the more "real" it becomes within the map.
Emergent Coherence (the Duck Principle) — when patterns across layers align harmonically, something coherent "wakes up" — that alignment moment is the "quack."
TL;DR at the bottom: Duckspace is a relational field where structure, energy, meaning, and feeling self-organize until something real enough to act emerges.

